{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0409"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge music-stage/instruments","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/music-stage__instruments.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",793],["+"," Singers are counted the same way: a duet is for two voices, a terzetto (German: Terzett) for three – so whoever sings in a terzetto has exactly 2 fellow singers – and a vocal quartet for four. Opera loves these numbers; the farewell terzettino \"Soave sia il vento\" in Mozart's \"Così fan tutte\" (1790) is one of the best known."],["=",292]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",156],["-","20."],["+","zwanzigsten"],["=",572],["+"," Sänger werden ebenso gezählt: Ein Duett ist für zwei Stimmen, ein Terzett für drei – wer im Terzett singt, hat also genau 2 Mitsänger – und ein Vokalquartett für vier. Die Oper liebt diese Nummern; das Abschiedsterzettino „Soave sia il vento“ aus Mozarts „Così fan tutte“ (1790) gehört zu den bekanntesten."],["=",254]]}]},
